.TH "CSSROTATE.X" "3JS" "September 10, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSRotate.x \- CSSRotate: x property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]x\f[B]\f[R] property of the \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R]
interface represents the x\-coordinate of the vector denoting the axis
of rotation.
.SH VALUE
A \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R].
If set to a number, this is wrapped in a \f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] of
\f[CR]unit: \(dqnumber\(dq\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Reading and setting the rotation axis
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] rotate = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSRotate(1, 1, 0, CSS.deg(45));

console.log(rotate.x.value); \f[I]// 1\f[R]

rotate.x = 0;
console.log(rotate.x); \f[I]// CSSUnitValue {value: 0, unit: \(dqnumber\(dq}\f[R]
.EE
